From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: denfry <dabinayo@pm.me>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 08:55:23 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Borrow regions for tasks of plugins in compatibility mode

While the global tick runs BukkitScheduler tasks of plugins in
compatibility mode, a failed thread check borrows the region owning the
chunk: the region is marked as ticking, the way unloading a world takes
regions, and becomes the current region of the global tick thread, so
the task works on it as if it ran in that region's tick. Every borrowed
region is released when the tasks finish. Waiting for a region that is
ticking right now is limited to 500 ms.

A scheduled tick or task run of a borrowed region is skipped instead of
failing with "Scheduled region should be acquirable", and the tick is
retried a millisecond later. Delay-0 tasks queued while plugins enable
now run on the first global tick instead of the startup thread, where
they could not borrow regions.

